## Visual concept used
A **provisioning depot / burn-rate metering ledger** — a brand-new sub-archetype within the locked "Engineering Diagnostic Instrument" style, and the first/only logistics-and-money-axis instrument in the Fit set. Read left → right as one supply line whose axis is **money/units, not time** (time appears only as small run-out flags). **THE HEAD** is the *planning manifest* (Step ①) — a clipboard listing every money-drawing variable (compounds, ancillary tiers, bloodwork, monitoring gear, daily consumables) with fold-out amber `IF X → +RM Y` contingency tabs and the two-documents lockup (budgeting plan + stock plan). **THE BODY** is the *bulk reservoir bank* (Steps ②–③): eight transparent stock tanks where **fill height = the one-time cart** and **spout width = the true monthly burn**, governed by the engraved brass law `MONTHLY = (CART ÷ SUPPLY-DAYS) × 30`. The protective core (rosuvastatin, aspirin) is drawn **tall-tank / hair-spout** — the visual punchline that the gear is *cheap per month*; tablet-splitters clamp the splittable tanks (10→5 mg, 50→25) halving the spout and doubling the run-out; TUDCA+NAC is a situational tank with its valve drawn **closed**, TEST a **seasonal** tank, bloodwork a **metered service** gauge. **THE SIGNATURE DEVICE** (right column, top) is the **receipt-vs-meter paradox**: a tall alarming amber `RM500–600` receipt column ("WHAT YOU BRACE FOR") collapsing through the burn-rate arrow (`÷ supply-days × 30`) into a thread-thin green `~RM60–80/mo` drip ("WHAT ACTUALLY RECURS"), stamped *the receipt is paid once; the meter is the bill*. **THE TAIL** (right column, bottom) is the **inverted monthly-outflow ledger** (Step ④): bars sized by what actually leaves the account — **FOOD** the dominant gushing bar, then GYM + consumables, then bloodwork, then the **PHARMA CORE as the thinnest trickle**, set over a ghosted "what you EXPECTED" (gear-huge) silhouette, under the law `FOOD ≫ GYM + CONSUMABLES > BLOODWORK > PHARMA CORE`. **THE ONE RED OBJECT** is the **food-readiness interlock** — a STOP gate on the FOOD bar ("if the food budget scares you, you're not ready for the gear"). A **capstone ribbon** compresses the whole 15-article spine into `DECIDE → SCREEN → MONITOR → OPTIMIZE → PROTECT → ASSEMBLE → ▣ BUDGET` (BUDGET lit as the terminal node), beside the `① SHIELD → ② GEAR → ③ MONITORING/CONSUMABLES` stocking order. Color rationed exactly per the brief: **ledger-green** for money that actually flows monthly (FOOD greenest, pharma barely tinted), **amber** for every contingency / sticker-shock / situational-valve state, **exactly one red** (the food interlock), ghosted grey for the corrected wrong-intuition silhouette. Distinct from 5.1's time-axis run-up trace and 3.2's annual Gantt.

